null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4456761762","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108847#issuecomment-4456761762","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108847","id":4456761762,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCaTJog","user":{"login":"Yandall","id":49245907,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MjQ1OTA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49245907?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall","html_url":"https://github.com/Yandall","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-15T03:58:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-15T03:58:00Z","body":"I think I'm having a related issue.\nI'm trying to show/hide instances in a compute shader changing the scale to 0 or 1 but that is not being reflected in the actual instances, the actual position is, but the scale is not so a instance could be in a permanent state of visibility.\nIf I use the workaround above to sync the buffer in the CPU then it works correctly\n```gdscript\nvar buffer_rid = RenderingServer.multimesh_get_buffer_rd_rid(multimesh.get_rid())\nvar buffer = rd.buffer_get_data(buffer_rid).to_float32_array()\nRenderingServer.multimesh_set_buffer(multimesh.get_rid(), buffer)\n```\n\nI'll prefer not to sync the buffer in CPU as it quickly becomes a bottleneck reading the buffer every frame. But at the same time I feel like I'm doing something wrong here","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4456761762/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4467417684","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108847#issuecomment-4467417684","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108847","id":4467417684,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCkdiVA","user":{"login":"natstott","id":59363512,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MzYzNTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59363512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott","html_url":"https://github.com/natstott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-16T16:22:24Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T16:22:24Z","body":"> I think I'm having a related issue. I'm trying to show/hide instances in a compute shader changing the scale to 0 or 1 but that is not being reflected in the actual instances, the actual position is, but the scale is not so a instance could be in a permanent state of visibility. If I use the workaround above to sync the buffer in the CPU then it works correctly\n> \n\nI can't see any reason why once you write to the buffer on the GPU, using compute shader, that it wouldn't be readable from any other shader on the GPU - providing you are running the compute shader in the render thread and not using a standalone renderingdevice. It sounds like you are for RenderingDevice.\n\nWhere are you reading back the changed scale? Are you able to change other values such as a the transform or custom values or is nothing working?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4467417684/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4467699605","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108847#issuecomment-4467699605","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108847","id":4467699605,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCkuvlQ","user":{"login":"Yandall","id":49245907,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MjQ1OTA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49245907?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall","html_url":"https://github.com/Yandall","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yandall/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-16T18:04:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-16T18:11:02Z","body":"> I can't see any reason why once you write to the buffer on the GPU, using compute shader, that it wouldn't be readable from any other shader on the GPU\n\nI think I explained my self very poorly. My issue is this: I initialized the multimesh buffer with all 0s (so the scale is 0 meaning no instances would be visible in the screen), then in a compute shader I update the buffer changing the scale from 0 to 1 (making it visible). Now here comes the issue, the instances are not visible in the screen even though the buffer is being updated correctly, and how do I know that the buffer is being updated correctly? By manually syncing the buffer in the CPU like this . Then I can see my instances and how the GPU is manipulating the buffer\n```gdscript\nvar buffer_rid = RenderingServer.multimesh_get_buffer_rd_rid(multimesh.get_rid())\nvar buffer = rd.buffer_get_data(buffer_rid).to_float32_array()\nRenderingServer.multimesh_set_buffer(multimesh.get_rid(), buffer)\n```\n\n> Are you able to change other values such as a the transform or custom values or is nothing working?\n\nYes, the origin, the custom color, and custom data is working correctly, is only the scale that is causing me trouble.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4467699605/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4469656458","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108847#issuecomment-4469656458","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108847","id":4469656458,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCmmLig","user":{"login":"natstott","id":59363512,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MzYzNTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59363512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott","html_url":"https://github.com/natstott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/natstott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-17T06:56:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-17T06:56:35Z","body":"I suspect multimesh hides instances that have zero size through some other hidden variable that is updated when the CPU writes the buffer. You could try creating them full size and reducing the scale in the shader to see if it works that way round. You should probably start a discussion in the forum rather than here.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4469656458/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]